Sval: a window's popups stay inside the window

Every menu, panel and tooltip a Sval window opens stays inside that
window: one that reaches past an edge flips, slides or shrinks to fit,
and its content scrolls. nsMenuPopupFrame::GetConstraintRect constrains
a chrome popup to the screen alone, so a popover could run off the
window and over the system's Dock; this adds the window's own rect, as
a content shell's popups already have, inset from the window's edges by
ui.popup.window_inset so a popup never meets an edge exactly. A popup
can still reach as far as its anchor does, so one that grows from a
button nearer an edge than the inset lines up with the button. The input
margin, the room a popup keeps for its shadow, may still reach past it.

diff --git a/layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp b/layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp
index a7b2131ceb..6efd0f9b83 100644
--- a/layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp
+++ b/layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp
@@ -1906,7 +1906,22 @@ Maybe<nsRect> nsMenuPopupFrame::GetConstraintRect(
   if (mInContentShell) {
     // For content shells, clip to the client area rather than the screen area
     AddConstraint(aRootScreenRect);
-  } else if (!mOverrideConstraintRect.IsEmpty()) {
+  } else if (pc->IsChrome()) {
+    // A chrome window's popups stay inside the window too, inset from its
+    // edges.
+    nsRect window = aRootScreenRect;
+    const nscoord inset = nsPresContext::CSSPixelsToAppUnits(
+        int32_t(StaticPrefs::ui_popup_window_inset()));
+    if (window.width > 2 * inset && window.height > 2 * inset) {
+      window.Deflate(inset);
+    }
+    // A popup can still line up with an anchor that stands nearer an edge.
+    if (!aAnchorRect.IsEmpty()) {
+      window = window.UnionEdges(aAnchorRect.Intersect(aRootScreenRect));
+    }
+    AddConstraint(window);
+  }
+  if (!mInContentShell && !mOverrideConstraintRect.IsEmpty()) {
     AddConstraint(mOverrideConstraintRect);
     // This is currently only used for <select> elements where we want to
     // constrain vertically to the screen but not horizontally, so do the
diff --git a/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml b/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
index da1da960c6..bd19305f0f 100644
--- a/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
+++ b/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
@@ -19569,6 +19569,12 @@
   value: false
   mirror: always
 
+# How far inside its chrome window's edges a popup stays, in CSS pixels.
+- name: ui.popup.window_inset
+  type: uint32_t
+  value: 0
+  mirror: always
+
 # Negate scroll, true will make the mouse scroll wheel move the screen the
 # same direction as with most desktops or laptops.
 - name: ui.scrolling.negate_wheel_scroll
